# Clio is the scope source of truth — check it before adding UI

Before adding ANY new control, card, button, panel, or "helper" UI to a page,
consult the Clio reference first. Clio (draft.clio.com) is the product we are
matching. If Clio does not have it on that page, default to NOT adding it.
Do not invent workflow chrome, status pills, "go to X" CTAs, rescan/debug
buttons, or duplicate navigation. Less is correct.

## Where to look (in this repo)

- Screenshots: `DESIGN SPECS/clio-screenshots/` (00–21). Key pages:
  - `08-panels-populate.png` → the fill-out / populate experience
  - `06-project-edit.png`, `09-panels-edit.png` → edit / overlay + sign
  - `05-project-overview.png`, `01-clients-active.png`, `02-clients-projects.png`
  - `17-form-libraries.png`, `20-sort-menu.png`, `21-select-court.png`
  - See `DESIGN SPECS/clio-screenshots/README.md` for the full index.
- Written audit: `DESIGN SPECS/DRAFT_CLIO_UI_DEEP_DIVE.md`
- Gap analysis: `DESIGN SPECS/DRAFT_CLIO_VS_PDFTIMESAVER_COMPARISON.md`

## Process for any UI change

1. Identify which page/flow you are touching.
2. Open the matching Clio screenshot(s) + the relevant deep-dive section.
3. Only add elements that exist in (or are clearly implied by) the Clio reference,
   or that the user explicitly requested in this conversation.
4. If something seems needed but isn't in Clio and wasn't requested, ASK before
   adding it — don't add speculatively.

## Known scope facts (don't re-add)

- Populate = panel/field fill only. No drafting CTA, no "Project Forms (Ordered)"
  table, no Populate/Drafting/Download workflow pills, no "Rescan PDF Fields".
- Download/export lives in the action bar, not as a separate workflow step card.

## Clio's actual panel split (verified 2026-06-19 against real logged-in panels)

- **Populate (`08`)** = pure data entry. One centered single-column card, logical
  fields grouped by section (Attorney / Client / Court / Other). Each input has a
  `×N` badge = how many PDF spots that one value fills (dedup). In Clio there are NO
  font controls, NO color, NO bold/underline/strikeout, NO custom-field placement,
  NO PDF preview, NO export controls on this page. Actions: Back to select documents,
  Go to drafting.
- **Drafting / Edit (`09`)** = the visual layer. `Insert → Add custom field`, live PDF
  overlay with stamped values, `Documents (N)` list to switch forms, status dropdown
  (In progress / Review / Completed), `Sign`, `Download`.
- Mental model: **Populate = data, Drafting/Edit = visual + custom fields + sign +
  download.** Our build intentionally diverges (font/color/custom-input/export on
  populate) per explicit user request — keep that, but don't add MORE visual chrome
  to populate without asking.
